# Non-blocking UI (API calls)

**Mandate:** network work must not freeze or blank the UI. Paint the shell immediately; run fetches in the background. Block only when the user cannot proceed without that result.

## Default (non-blocking)

- Hydrate from localStorage / IndexedDB / in-memory cache first; revalidate in the background.
- Show chrome + skeletons/stale data while requests run. Never `if (loading) return` a full-page spinner for auth or secondary data when a cached user/session exists.
- Prefer `Promise.all` / `allSettled` for independent calls. Do not waterfall A→B→C when A and B are independent.
- Mutations (star, complete, rename, planner toggle, delete-from-list): optimistic update, then API, rollback on failure.
- Navigation (Ask AI, open page): route immediately; create/fetch on the destination if needed.
- Popovers/search: prefetch or reuse cache; do not refetch-on-open as the only source of the badge/list.
- Overlays that steal pointer events are forbidden on refetch when the view already has data.

## When blocking is allowed

- Credential submit (login/register) until success/error.
- First paint of a document that has no cached bytes/metadata (reader content area only — chrome can still show).
- Waiting for a user-initiated AI stream/answer the user asked to see.
- Destructive confirm that must finish before leaving a screen, if rollback is impossible.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — whole page waits on /me
if (authLoading || !user) return <FullPageSpinner />;

// ✅ GOOD — stored user paints now; /me refreshes later
const stored = getStoredUser();
if (stored) { setUser(stored); void api.auth.me().then(...) }

// ❌ BAD — overlay on every listTasks()
{tasksLoading && <div className="absolute inset-0">Loading</div>}

// ✅ GOOD
{tasksLoading && tasks.length === 0 && <PlannerSkeleton />}
```
